## 🛆 Import Convention

```ts
// External
import React from 'react';
// Extension UI
import { Button, Input } from '@extension/ui/components';
// Extension Hooks
import { useAppInitialization } from '@extension/hooks';
// Common Services
import { cardValidationService } from '@common/core/services';
// Common Libraries
import { getPlatformAdapter } from '@common/core/adapters';
// Types
import type { CardFormData } from '@common/types';
```

* Always use absolute imports (`@common`, `@extension`)
* Never use relative imports like `../../../`
* Group by layer in order: external → extension UI → extension hooks → common services → common libraries → types

---

## 📊 State & Data Flow

* UI reads only from Zustand and secure local storage
* Never access Firestore, local storage, or platform APIs in hooks or pages
* Platform adapters hydrate vault and handle local persistence
* All decrypted data lives in RAM only and never persisted
* `logout()` must wipe all memory state and secure storage
* Extension uses Chrome storage APIs for persistence

---

## 🔐 Secure Storage (Chrome Extension)

* Use `chrome.storage.session` for temporary data
* Use `chrome.storage.local` for persistent data (encrypted)
* Never store plaintext passwords or sensitive data
* All sensitive data must be encrypted before storage
* Use extension-specific storage adapters in `packages/extension/adapters/`

---

## 🎨 Styling Rules (DOM Components)

* Use CSS-in-JS or inline styles for extension components
* Use only `gap` for vertical spacing (not `marginTop`/`marginBottom`)
* Layout classes: `formContainer`, `scrollView`, `pageContainer`, etc.
* No inline spacing logic — always through centralized layout system
* Ensure components work in Chrome extension popup and content script contexts
* Use semantic HTML elements for accessibility

---

## 🛍️ Navigation (Routing) Rules

* Navigation must only occur from hooks or UI using the `useAppRouterContext()`
* Do not pass fallback callbacks (e.g., `onSuccess`) — use router directly
* Pages should not perform navigation decisions
* Routing must remain testable and explicit
* Routes must be declared in one central place (router file)
* Extension routing should be DOM-based, not React Native Web

---

## 🏗️ Build & Validation Checklist

After any structural or logic-level change:

```bash
npm run lint:extension
npm run test:extension
npm run build:extension
npm run type-check:extension
```

* All tests must pass
* TypeScript build must succeed
* > 80% test coverage for business logic
* No ESLint/TypeScript warnings
* Must follow 3-layer separation strictly
* Extension must build successfully with Vite

---

## 🚀 Extension-Specific Rules

### Chrome Extension Development
* Use React DOM components, not React Native Web
* Follow Chrome extension manifest V3 requirements
* Ensure popup, content scripts, and background scripts work correctly
* Use extension-specific adapters for platform operations
* Test in actual Chrome extension environment

### Popover Development
* Popovers should be DOM-based and isolated
* Use extension-specific popover components
* Ensure proper security for content script injection
* Test autofill functionality thoroughly

### Security Considerations
* All user data must be encrypted before storage
* Content scripts must sanitize all input
* Never expose sensitive data in popup or content scripts
* Use secure communication between extension contexts

